---
import ShareLinks from '../../../components/ShareLinks.astro';
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Footer from '../../../components/Footer.astro';
import ToolVote from '../../../components/ToolVote.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Sammans"
  description="A coach for personal growth that makes your relationships stronger. It helps you find direction, set goals that survive an ordinary week and picks the tools – while the year wheel and everyday life stay where they are. Everything stays on the phone."
>
  <main class="reading" id="main">
    <section class="block insight-page">
      <p class="kicker"><a href="/tools/">Tools</a></p>
      <h1>Sammans</h1>

      <p class="lede">
        A good relationship isn't fixed. It's kept — with care and curiosity, a little every day.
      </p>

      <p>
        Sammans is a coach for personal growth that makes your relationships stronger. For couples who are doing
        well and want to keep it that way. Two minutes a day. You grow, and it shows at home.
      </p>

      <p>
        No partner right now? Use it on your own. Everything about you works the same, and the care goes to friends
        and family instead. Add a partner whenever you like — nothing you've done disappears.
      </p>

      <h2>A coach up front. A toolbox behind it.</h2>

      <p>
        Tell it what you need more of — calm, energy, closeness, focus. It helps you find a direction, a goal and
        the first small step. Then it picks the tools: mindful presence, mental strength, self-confidence, love as
        something you do.
      </p>

      <p>
        You don't have to know where to start. You can still open the toolbox yourself, any time.
      </p>

      <h2>Goals that survive an ordinary week</h2>

      <p>
        Why it matters to you. What in you might get in the way. A plan for when it does: <em>if I'm tired, then I
        do the five-minute version.</em> Small steps that go straight into your day.
      </p>

      <p>
        Every suggestion is a starting point, not a script. On Sunday the coach asks how it went and helps you
        choose next week's steps.
      </p>

      <h2>Your good days have something in common</h2>

      <p>A walk after dinner. An evening without phones. Laughing at the same thing in the kitchen.</p>

      <p>
        Sammans notices what your better days share. After two weeks it shows you — and asks how you'd like to
        make room for more of it.
      </p>

      <h2>Love is something you do</h2>

      <p>
        Alfred Adler saw love as one of life's great tasks. Not a feeling you fall into, but something two people do,
        every day, as equals.
      </p>

      <p>Warm the towels before they shower. Make the coffee the way they like it. Tell them why you chose them.</p>

      <p>
        Sixty steps like that, one at a time. Together they change how you are with each other.
      </p>

      <h2>Get to know each other again</h2>

      <p>If we had our own sitcom, what would it be called — and who would play us?</p>
      <p>What's your favourite dish right now? Is it the same as five years ago?</p>

      <p>
        People change. Curiosity keeps up. Sammans has questions to laugh at and questions that go a little deeper.
        It remembers the ones you liked, and new ones arrive now and then.
      </p>

      <h2>More of what's yours</h2>

      <p>
        Time for the two of you, booked before the week fills up. The long weekends it finds in the calendar. Shared
        dreams, a bucket list, the dinner you keep meaning to cook. Each other's love languages, so the care lands
        where it's meant to.
      </p>

      <h2>Brave conversations get easier</h2>

      <p>
        Even good couples have something they keep putting off. Sammans helps you bring it up while it's still small —
        and lets you practise the conversation first. Afterwards it asks how it felt. Often lighter than you thought.
      </p>

      <h2>See it</h2>

      <p>
        Nine screens from the app, with two weeks of made-up data. Two of them scroll the way you would.
      </p>
    </section>

    <div class="demo-wide">
      <iframe
        id="sammans-demo"
        src="/tools/sammans-demo.html"
        title="Sammans walkthrough"
        loading="lazy"
        scrolling="no"
      ></iframe>
      <p class="demo-fallback">
        <a href="/tools/sammans-demo.html">Open the walkthrough on its own</a>
      </p>
    </div>

    <section class="block insight-page">
      <h2>It remembers the good things for you</h2>

      <p>
        Your own words from a good evening. The steps that felt right. The days you did something together. Weeks
        later, it brings them back — so the good doesn't get lost in the busy.
      </p>

      <h2>Your whole life on one page</h2>

      <p>
        How you feel, the relationship, your growth and your goals — drawn as one wheel. Next to it, the life puzzle:
        the house, the boat, the dinners for the week, the birthdays coming up. The year wheel and the daily
        activities are still there, exactly where they were.
      </p>

      <h2>It stays on your phone</h2>

      <p>
        No account. No server of its own. What the two of you choose to share travels encrypted through your own
        iCloud. The diary, the energy and the personal parts never leave the device.
      </p>

      <p>
        Where the iPhone's own AI is on, you can talk things through with the coach. Where it's off, that button
        simply isn't there.
      </p>

      <p>
        It's coaching, not therapy, and it says so. With deeper obstacles — like anxiety or burnout — a therapist is
        the right help. If what you write sounds like a crisis, it stops coaching and shows you where to get support.
      </p>

      <h2>One subscription. Both of you.</h2>

      <p>
        Fourteen days free. Then 39 kr a month or 299 kr a year, shared through Family Sharing. Swedish and English.
        On its way to TestFlight — if you want in before the App Store, <a href="/contact/">write to me</a>.
      </p>

      <p>
        It replaces <a href="/tools/livspusslet/">Livspusslet</a>. The year, the food and the long weekends are still
        in there. They just come after you now.
      </p>

      <p class="closing">Love is kept, not fixed.</p>

      <ShareLinks title="Sammans — a TROi tool" />

      <ToolVote tool="sammans" />
    </section>
  </main>

  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .insight-page h2 {
    font-family: 'Fraunces', serif;
    font-weight: 500;
    font-size: 1.3rem;
    margin: 2.6rem 0 0.7rem;
  }
  .closing {
    font-family: 'Fraunces', serif;
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    margin: 2.4rem 0 2rem;
  }
  /* The walkthrough is wider than the reading measure, so it steps out of the
     column to the shell width the rest of the site uses. */
  .demo-wide {
    width: min(65rem, calc(100vw - 3rem));
    margin: 2rem 0 3.4rem 50%;
    transform: translateX(-50%);
  }
  @media (max-width: 40rem) {
    .demo-wide {
      width: calc(100vw - 2rem);
    }
  }
  .demo-wide iframe {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: 900px;
    border: 0;
  }
  .demo-fallback {
    margin: 0.6rem 0 0;
    font-family: 'Space Mono', monospace;
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }
</style>

<script>
  // Same-origin, so the height can be measured directly and the site's theme
  // toggle can be handed through to the frame.
  const frame = document.getElementById('sammans-demo') as HTMLIFrameElement | null;

  if (frame) {
    const syncTheme = () => {
      const doc = frame.contentDocument;
      if (!doc) return;
      const theme = document.documentElement.dataset.theme;
      if (theme) doc.documentElement.dataset.theme = theme;
      else delete doc.documentElement.dataset.theme;
    };

    const syncHeight = () => {
      const doc = frame.contentDocument;
      if (!doc?.body) return;
      frame.style.height = `${doc.body.scrollHeight + 8}px`;
    };

    const wire = () => {
      syncTheme();
      syncHeight();
      const doc = frame.contentDocument;
      if (doc?.body && 'ResizeObserver' in window) {
        new ResizeObserver(syncHeight).observe(doc.body);
      }
      // Each step's text is a different length.
      setInterval(syncHeight, 1000);
    };

    frame.addEventListener('load', wire);
    if (frame.contentDocument?.readyState === 'complete') wire();

    new MutationObserver(syncTheme).observe(document.documentElement, {
      attributes: true,
      attributeFilter: ['data-theme'],
    });
  }
</script>
